-names>S.S.</given-names></name><name><surname>Cho</surname><given-names>M.S.</given-names></name><name><surname>Kaplan</surname><given-names>D.</given-names></name><name><surname>Bhuva</surname><given-names>D.</given-names></name><name><surname>Malley</surname><given-names>J.</given-names></name><name><surname>Zimmerberg</surname><given-names>J.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The calcium sensitivity of individual secretory vesicles is invariant with the rate of calcium delivery</article-title><source>J. Gen. Phys.</source><volume>112</volume><year>1998</year><fpage>569</fpage><lpage>576</lpage>b</citation></ref><ref id="Bollmanetal2000"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bollman</surname><given-names>J.H.</given-names></name><name><surname>Sakman</surname><given-names>B.</given-names></name><name><surname>Borst</surname><given-names>J.G.G.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Calcium sensitivity of glutamate release in a calyx-type terminal</article-title><source>Science.</source><volume>289</volume><year>2000</year><fpage>953</fpage><lpage>957</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10937999</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="BorstandSakman1996"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Borst</surname><given-names>J.G.G.</given-names></name><name><surname>Sakman</surname><given-names>B.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Calcium influx and transmitter release in a fast CNS synapse</article-title><source>Nature.</source><volume>383</volume><year>1996</year><fpage>431</fpage><lpage>434</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8837774</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ChadandEckert1984"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Chad</surname><given-names>J.E.</given-names></name><name><surname>Eckert</surname><given-names>R.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Calcium doma